roughout the video.  detailed_description:\nThe target video is a photorealistic digital-human presentation matching the frame proportion and natural lighting and color of <Picture 1>, rendered with true-to-life skin texture, realistic pores, and continuous subtle facial micro-movements, so that every frame reads as footage of a real person captured by a real camera.\n[Shot 1] The shot begins exactly from <Picture 1>, preserving the subject's pose, scale, orientation, and framing, and the original background, lighting direction, shadows, color balance, depth of field, main light, fill light, back light, exposure, white balance, and lens height, all without redesigning or replacing them. <Subject 1> (S1) is positioned in frame exactly as in the reference image, wearing the identical face, hairstyle, makeup, clothing, and accessories from <Picture 1>, situated within <Subject 2>, the unchanged environment from <Picture 1>. The camera remains completely locked, with no pan, tilt, zoom, dolly, orbit, reframing, lens change, focus pulsing, or artificial camera shake. The camera must remain 100% physically static for the whole duration under all circumstances — no pan, tilt, zoom, dolly, orbit, reframing, lens change, focus drift, or shake of any kind; any camera motion is a defect. Within the first second, after a restrained natural inhale and with the gaze already steady on the camera, <Subject 1> (S1) begins speaking the complete spoken content of the platform runtime-driven audio, which is supplied by the platform at generation time as the final audio track. Every word, pause, breath, and intonation comes from the platform runtime-driven audio, and the lips, jaw, cheeks, tongue, and teeth of <Subject 1> (S1) follow the audio phonemes in precise synchronisation: the mouth begins moving exactly when the speech begins and stops precisely with the final spoken sound; the mouth movements stay natural and moderate in amplitude, never over-articulated and never exaggerated; during pauses the mouth stays naturally closed or relaxed. Bilabial consonants show a brief, accurate lip closure; labiodental sounds show the lower lip meeting the upper teeth; rounded vowels round the lips naturally; open vowels release through moderate jaw drop. Stressed syllables increase mouth and jaw amplitude slightly, while soft, low, or sentence-final passages reduce it. Lip motion connects smoothly between phrases without resetting per word, and the mouth never continues mouthing during silence, inhales, or non-speech pauses; the subject never invents or mouths extra words beyond the driving speech. Small authentic behaviors fill the gaps: realistic jaw movement, small cheek deformation, occasional natural blinking at a human rate, gentle eye movement, minimal eyebrow response, subtle breathing visible in the shoulders and chest, and restrained micro-expressions appropriate to the meaning and tone of the speech. Micro-expressions follow a subtle-appear, moderate-emphasis, natural-settle pattern; avoid a fixed smile, instant face change, permanently open mouth, or stiff ad-model stiffness. <Subject 1> (S1) keeps steady, natural eye contact with the camera without an unnaturally fixed stare. While speaking, <Subject 1> (S1) occasionally raises one hand and makes small, calm, meaningful gestures that support the content being spoken, then returns the hand to rest; if the hands are visible, their appearance and position are preserved with only minimal natural movement. The collar, fabric texture, buttons, accessories, and pendant stay stable, shifting only minimally with natural breathing; they must not float, clip through the body, or deform. The facial expression remains genuine, warm, and composed throughout. Do not introduce new people, objects, animals, visible text, subtitles, logos, scene transitions, visual effects, or any stray floating elements such as particles, light spots, snow, specks, dust, or bokeh, lens flare, light leak, local brightness pulsation, color flicker, or random shadow that are not present in <Picture 1>. Every visual element in the frame must belong to <Picture 1> and obey ordinary physical reality; any visible text, logo, or watermark already present in <Picture 1> stays anchored to its original surface position and must not drift, deform, or be re-spelled; nothing should drift, flicker, sparkle, or appear that is absent from the reference image. The video ends on the final syllable of the platform runtime-driven audio as <Subject 1> (S1) settles into a relaxed, natural resting expression, still framed exactly like <Picture 1>.  overall_soundscape:\nThe audible sound of the target video is provided entirely by the platform runtime-driven audio: the subject's speech, breaths, and natural pauses exactly as supplied by the input driving speech, with no additional sound effects layered on top. Any music or ambient sound already present in the input audio is treated as part of the input and is not regenerated; all vocal, breath, and micro-expression energy follows the platform runtime-driven audio timeline, and no second voice, narration, singing, or harmony is added.  non_diegetic_music:\nN/A"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "label": "prompt", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "提示词"}], "flags": {}, "type": "CR Prompt Text", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [314.6971740722656, 108], "pos": [7592.18408203125, 463.62652587890625], "id": 72, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "CR Prompt Text"}, "order": 11}], "extra": {"links_added_by_ue": [], "VHS_KeepIntermediate": true, "KKvideo_latentpreview": false, "ue_links": [], "KKvideo_latentpreviewrate": 0, "VHS_MetadataImage": true, "0246.VERSION": [0, 0, 4], "pixaromaGroups": [], "VHS_latentpreviewrate": 0, "frontendVersion": "1.23.0", "VHS_latentpreview": false, "ds": {"offset": [-1436.028730762503, 854.8677111471598], "scale": 0.2794145953766199}}, "groups": [{"color": "#3f789e", "fon